WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:15.038 --> 00:00:19.461
Of all the forms of fighting known to man,
one name strikes fear further into the

00:00:19.481 --> 00:00:20.602
hearts of those who hear it.

00:00:21.202 --> 00:00:21.902
Bare Knuckle.

00:00:24.452 --> 00:00:29.074
For hundreds of years, the men of Britain
have rammed their unprotected fists into

00:00:29.134 --> 00:00:31.255
each other's bodies to decide who was the

00:00:31.295 --> 00:00:32.015
hardest of them all.

00:00:37.538 --> 00:00:43.040
From noblemen, to travellers, to family
men and gangsters, being a bare knuckle

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.341
fighter is something that

00:00:44.381 --> 00:00:46.302
marks you out from the rest of society.

00:00:48.943 --> 00:00:50.504
It's a thoroughly British blood sport.

00:00:50.844 --> 00:00:54.205
that gradually sank further into the
criminal underground as the rest of

00:00:54.225 --> 00:00:56.165
society became more civilised.

00:00:57.786 --> 00:01:01.327
It's a sport of legend, honour and
astonishing violence.

00:01:05.368 --> 00:01:09.509
Bare Knuckle Fighting is a world that most
people think they understand, but few have

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:10.269
actually seen.

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:15.631
Now, a number of fighters and promoters
are trying to take it into the mainstream,

00:01:15.991 --> 00:01:18.632
setting up the most anticipated Bare
Knuckle Fight in

00:01:18.652 --> 00:01:19.852
over 150 years.

00:01:20.432 --> 00:01:21.952
America versus Britain.

00:01:22.773 --> 00:01:27.074
And I wanted to know if the sport can ever
truly take itself out of its underground

00:01:27.114 --> 00:01:27.814
past.

00:01:42.458 --> 00:01:46.359
The common perception of bare knuckle
fighting is that only Irish travellers and

00:01:46.379 --> 00:01:47.620
East End hard men still do it.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:48.740
But in actual fact...

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:52.522
they're still a thriving underground and
the fighters come from all walks of life.

00:01:53.063 --> 00:01:55.264
And it originates here in the UK.

00:01:56.145 --> 00:01:59.027
I'm here in Hinkley just outside Leicester
to meet Andy Topliff.

00:01:59.527 --> 00:02:04.711
Now Andy runs a promotion company called
Be Bad Promotions and what he aims to do

00:02:04.771 --> 00:02:06.452
with that company is to

00:02:06.692 --> 00:02:08.894
kind of bring bare knuckle into the
mainstream.

00:02:09.214 --> 00:02:14.058
It's an up and coming fight company and I
do it because I love the sport and I want

00:02:14.059 --> 00:02:14.759
the sport to grow.

00:02:15.439 --> 00:02:18.648
Intrigued to know more about the history
of bare knuckle, and why now it seems to

00:02:18.649 --> 00:02:22.109
be on the up, we met at a patriotic pub
just outside Leicester.

00:02:22.529 --> 00:02:23.229
Andy, how's it going?

00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:24.270
Nice to meet you.

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:25.030
Hey, how are you?

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:29.011
What is the history of bare knuckle
fighting in England and Britain?

00:02:29.431 --> 00:02:35.253
Bare knuckle fighting as a sport was
absolutely categorically English.

00:02:35.373 --> 00:02:36.393
It was an English thing.

00:02:36.833 --> 00:02:41.134
The Europeans feared Englishmen for their
fighting ability.

00:02:41.555 --> 00:02:44.695
It's actually a British heritage, bare
knuckle fighting is.

00:02:44.915 --> 00:02:46.596
It's where boxing comes from.

00:02:47.144 --> 00:02:50.705
Certainly in the 18th century, very, very
big sport.

00:02:51.166 --> 00:02:55.007
Even the royal family, they would want to
know who won, you know, if it was a big

00:02:55.047 --> 00:02:55.747
fight.

00:02:55.747 --> 00:02:56.948
They were like superstars of today.

00:02:57.628 --> 00:02:58.749
And how about your own background?

00:02:58.769 --> 00:03:00.089
How did you get into bare knuckle?

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:02.930
From a very young age, to be honest with
you.

00:03:02.931 --> 00:03:05.391
You know, I was brought up in the
travelling community.

00:03:05.832 --> 00:03:07.993
My hands, they're destroyed basically now.

00:03:08.393 --> 00:03:09.813
They're deformed because of it.

00:03:10.053 --> 00:03:15.315
Obviously in the bare knuckle world, there
has always been quite a lot of input with

00:03:15.335 --> 00:03:16.035
criminals.

00:03:16.035 --> 00:03:16.596
Do you know what I mean?

00:03:16.676 --> 00:03:18.077
I wanted to push all of that out.

00:03:18.437 --> 00:03:19.678
I wanted that gone.

00:03:20.198 --> 00:03:24.862
You know, I decided to do B-Bad and keep
it as a proper sport.

00:03:25.202 --> 00:03:28.324
I really want to get this regulated and
get it mainstream.

00:03:28.584 --> 00:03:32.467
We started the first UK belt since, you
know, way over 100 years.

00:03:32.587 --> 00:03:37.630
And then I thought, well, one extra step
and we'll go for the Atlantic belt, which

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.891
is a real historic event.

00:03:39.312 --> 00:03:42.974
I'd always wanted to get, you know, an
American to come over.

00:03:43.915 --> 00:03:45.436
Jason Young, this is the man.

00:03:45.716 --> 00:03:48.177
who I've dreamt of getting over into this
country.

00:03:48.577 --> 00:03:50.577
We're making history with this guy being
here.

00:03:50.757 --> 00:03:56.259
The last time an American was in this
country fighting for a belt, you know,

00:03:56.299 --> 00:03:57.519
against a UK champion,

00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:59.300
1863.

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:00.020
It's a big deal.

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:04.361
Jason had flown into the UK prior to the
fight and had surrounded himself with some

00:04:04.362 --> 00:04:07.062
of the most knowledgeable fighters in the
UK, including

00:04:07.162 --> 00:04:11.563
ex-Bare Knuckle champion Paddy Monaghan,
famous for his friendship with Muhammad

00:04:11.623 --> 00:04:12.323
Ali.

00:04:12.323 --> 00:04:14.364
Three years it took us to get you here,
didn't it?

00:04:14.365 --> 00:04:15.204
Three years, but I'm here.

00:04:16.365 --> 00:04:17.065
No excuses.

00:04:17.065 --> 00:04:17.826
No excuses, that's it.

00:04:17.827 --> 00:04:18.527
I'm here.

00:04:18.527 --> 00:04:20.387
And you're gonna prove the boys wrong,
innit, eh?

00:04:20.388 --> 00:04:21.168
Oh yeah.

00:04:21.169 --> 00:04:24.670
But he couldn't stick around for long, as
he was off to Wing Chun Grand Master

00:04:24.791 --> 00:04:28.153
Samuel Kwok's martial arts retreat in
Blackpool, a man

00:04:28.154 --> 00:04:30.074
who apparently once trained with Bruce
Lee.

00:04:31.795 --> 00:04:34.197
Clearly, Jason was taking this fight very
seriously.

00:04:37.059 --> 00:04:40.562
But whilst my own experiences of fighting
are fairly pathetic, I was intrigued to

00:04:40.582 --> 00:04:43.904
meet a man who'd been fighting since the
age of 10, James .

00:04:44.144 --> 00:04:46.030
Gypsy Boy McCrory from Newcastle.

00:04:46.591 --> 00:04:48.236
A living legend in the bare knuckle scene.

00:04:48.614 --> 00:04:51.916
and the man pitted up against Jason Young
in the Atlantic title fight.

00:04:54.238 --> 00:04:58.521
We met him at his local haunt, a 50s
themed diner in the centre of town.

00:04:59.241 --> 00:05:00.342
So what's good here?

00:05:00.362 --> 00:05:02.043
Everything is good, but the burgers are
huge.

00:05:02.463 --> 00:05:04.405
The reason why I come here is because we
were told to bring this here.

00:05:04.406 --> 00:05:06.906
If we had just come here, they wouldn't
sell beer, you know what I mean?

00:05:06.986 --> 00:05:07.887
So that's the truth.

00:05:08.888 --> 00:05:10.509
Your nickname is Gypsy Boy.

00:05:10.609 --> 00:05:11.309
Where does that come from?

00:05:11.669 --> 00:05:12.750
Obviously I've travelled all over.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:15.132
I've lived in Ireland and worked all over.

00:05:15.652 --> 00:05:18.174
Is being Irish a big part of your fighting
heritage?

00:05:18.658 --> 00:05:21.199
Yeah, I love Ireland.

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:23.181
I love going back there, I love seeing my
mum.

00:05:23.182 --> 00:05:24.021
I love it.

00:05:24.521 --> 00:05:26.302
I love spending time with my family,
honestly.

00:05:26.522 --> 00:05:29.644
I love sitting in the city, like, cuddle,
watching TV, me.

00:05:29.844 --> 00:05:30.725
Big softie.

00:05:30.765 --> 00:05:31.465
Love my family.

00:05:33.386 --> 00:05:37.648
You know, loads of people, they treat me,
get full of rides and all that crap, but I

00:05:37.649 --> 00:05:40.310
prefer to get full of Guinness and full

00:05:40.311 --> 00:05:41.011
of food, you know.

00:05:41.011 --> 00:05:43.031
It's a much more fun way of doing it.

00:05:43.032 --> 00:05:43.732
Yeah.

00:05:43.732 --> 00:05:46.313
My days have been a model of well gone, so
don't worry about the old six pack

00:05:46.333 --> 00:05:47.033
anymore, me.

00:05:47.033 --> 00:05:47.674
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:47.675 --> 00:05:48.375
You've got the cake.

00:05:48.375 --> 00:05:49.811
That's it, I've got a full keg now.

00:05:51.572 --> 00:05:56.154
James, a self-professed softie and family
man, invited us to his house to meet his

00:05:56.194 --> 00:05:58.135
charming and long-suffering girlfriend,

00:05:58.455 --> 00:05:59.456
Leanne.

00:05:59.457 --> 00:06:01.037
I love being the life and soul of the
party, you know.

00:06:01.038 --> 00:06:04.659
I'm Jack the lad, but then you don't know
where my bread's about, I don't know what

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:06.900
I mean, and I've got a good girl and she's
put up with a lot.

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:09.782
Hopefully one day I'll marry her late, you
know.

00:06:10.642 --> 00:06:11.342
What does she do?

00:06:11.523 --> 00:06:12.963
Drives me fucking bonkers, you know.

00:06:17.025 --> 00:06:17.725
Howdy toots.

00:06:20.162 --> 00:06:21.082
How are you doing lads?

00:06:21.083 --> 00:06:22.543
Yeah.

00:06:22.544 --> 00:06:23.303
Hey, how's it going?

00:06:23.304 --> 00:06:24.323
How's life?

00:06:24.324 --> 00:06:25.684
Do you want a cup of?

00:06:25.685 --> 00:06:26.484
I'm alright, I'm fine.

00:06:26.864 --> 00:06:28.705
Me and James are very, very different.

00:06:29.245 --> 00:06:34.446
Like, you couldn't get two people more
different in regards to what we're like,

00:06:35.046 --> 00:06:35.746
how we've lived our

00:06:35.767 --> 00:06:37.707
lives, the choices we've made.

00:06:38.347 --> 00:06:40.888
How do you feel about him being considered
a legend?

00:06:42.729 --> 00:06:43.449
Erm, I find it funny.

00:06:44.129 --> 00:06:45.209
Because it's James.

00:06:45.789 --> 00:06:47.270
He gets fan mail now.

00:06:48.334 --> 00:06:50.375
Which is quite funny.

00:06:50.376 --> 00:06:57.078
The person you see on the fights on
YouTube, that's not him.

00:06:57.358 --> 00:07:00.319
I know it is, but that's not the person I
know.

00:07:01.159 --> 00:07:02.720
I don't like it, to be honest with you.

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:07.502
When you come back from the Dave Radcliffe
fight, his face was really bad.

00:07:08.282 --> 00:07:09.762
There was blood on my pillow.

00:07:09.782 --> 00:07:11.923
I cleaned them the next morning.

00:07:11.924 --> 00:07:13.384
I thought there was some more blood on the
pillowcase.

00:07:13.385 --> 00:07:14.664
I thought I washed the doorway twice.

00:07:15.304 --> 00:07:16.625
There was blood on the pillowcase.

00:07:16.626 --> 00:07:17.705
It was just awful.

00:07:18.085 --> 00:07:22.647
It's not just about him having a fight,
it's the effect that it can have on us in

00:07:22.667 --> 00:07:23.567
regards as a couple.

00:07:23.767 --> 00:07:25.167
Build up to certain fights.

00:07:25.168 --> 00:07:26.488
It's like a time bomb.

00:07:26.548 --> 00:07:30.309
Last summer I had a bit of a bad time and
I thought, you know, this is not working.

00:07:30.369 --> 00:07:31.509
I'm away.

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:32.830
But...

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:37.973
I've never seen anybody fight as much as
what he did to get me back.

00:07:44.759 --> 00:07:47.821
Having learnt about the origins of Bare
Knuckle and spent time with some of the

00:07:47.841 --> 00:07:50.724
biggest names in the game, it was time to
see it in the flesh.

00:07:51.384 --> 00:07:54.647
B-Bab was holding an event in Colwyn Bay,
North Wales.

00:07:56.368 --> 00:07:59.871
The first fight between a pair of
seemingly well-matched middleweights was

00:07:59.951 --> 00:08:00.752
over in seconds.

00:08:03.806 --> 00:08:07.570
The second and last fight of the night was
something that will stay with me forever.

00:08:11.514 --> 00:08:16.558
Seth Jones, a 46 year old local solicitor
and lunatic known as the Bangor Hammer,

00:08:17.099 --> 00:08:18.260
took on a man 20 years

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:21.964
younger than himself only to go the
distance in a fight that was as

00:08:22.004 --> 00:08:23.725
controversial as it was thrilling.

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:56.232
The solicitor was bending the rules
somewhat.

00:08:56.452 --> 00:08:57.253
Stop him when you know he's coming for
you.

00:08:57.254 --> 00:08:58.734
Give up now, Stokes Come on Come on Come
on Come on Come on Come on Come on Come on

00:08:58.735 --> 00:09:03.879
Come on Come on Come on Come on Come

00:09:07.502 --> 00:09:08.202
on

00:09:15.369 --> 00:09:17.791
Come on Come on Come on Come on Come on
Come on Come on Come on Come on Come on

00:09:17.792 --> 00:09:18.492
Come on

00:09:22.142 --> 00:09:26.524
It seemed odd to see so much blood in what
was supposedly a stalemate, but I couldn't

00:09:26.564 --> 00:09:27.304
call a winner either.

00:09:28.585 --> 00:09:31.786
Seth seemed like he'd taken more abuse,
but Aaron looked exhausted.

00:09:33.707 --> 00:09:34.648
It was my first fight.

00:09:34.708 --> 00:09:37.909
I put myself forwards for it when I saw it
on the internet for a 13 stone fighter.

00:09:38.289 --> 00:09:40.790
How does it feel fighting someone who's 20
years older than you?

00:09:41.411 --> 00:09:42.111
Don't really matter.

00:09:42.111 --> 00:09:45.453
I've had street fights with older people
since I've been young, you know what I

00:09:45.493 --> 00:09:46.193
mean?

00:09:46.213 --> 00:09:47.914
I used to get in trouble fighting and all
that lot.

00:09:48.614 --> 00:09:49.875
I think you're a more peaceful person.

00:09:50.055 --> 00:09:51.116
Yeah, I'm peaceful anyway.

00:09:51.196 --> 00:09:53.397
But you're also getting a lot of street
fights.

00:09:53.537 --> 00:09:54.778
How does that kind of work out?

00:09:54.779 --> 00:09:57.420
I used to get in street fights when I was
younger because I used to hang around with

00:09:57.421 --> 00:09:58.121
the wrong crowd.

00:09:58.600 --> 00:10:00.682
My genuineness was going a bit too much.

00:10:01.022 --> 00:10:04.304
Now I know how it feels, I can control it
a little bit more, I think, in my next

00:10:04.344 --> 00:10:05.044
fight.

00:10:05.044 --> 00:10:06.725
I couldn't see out of my left eye.

00:10:06.726 --> 00:10:07.426
I got poked in it.

00:10:07.766 --> 00:10:09.786
I think it's a good result from both of
us.

00:10:10.026 --> 00:10:10.887
I'm chuffed with it.

00:10:10.888 --> 00:10:11.707
How do you feel right now?

00:10:12.607 --> 00:10:13.307
Buzzing.

00:10:13.307 --> 00:10:14.787
Do you think you'll feel worse tomorrow
morning?

00:10:14.968 --> 00:10:15.668
You know what I mean?

00:10:15.668 --> 00:10:16.269
I've had worse than this.

00:10:16.269 --> 00:10:16.889
Yeah?

00:10:16.889 --> 00:10:17.568
Yeah.

00:10:20.989 --> 00:10:25.010
How does it feel fighting guys who are,
what, considerably younger than you?

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:25.910
Half my age.

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:26.850
Half your age?

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:29.611
That's just the nature of bare-knuckle
boxing.

00:10:29.631 --> 00:10:31.431
I've fought guys older than myself.

00:10:31.711 --> 00:10:33.351
I don't mind fighting younger guys.

00:10:33.391 --> 00:10:34.091
I don't mind.

00:10:34.312 --> 00:10:35.252
I just like fighting.

00:10:35.932 --> 00:10:36.793
Do you fight in the streets?

00:10:37.233 --> 00:10:37.933
No, no.

00:10:37.994 --> 00:10:41.456
Them days, I used to have a lot of fights
when I was younger.

00:10:41.677 --> 00:10:45.980
Built up a bit of a reputation in the
area, but it was a huge mistake in my

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:46.740
life.

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:52.325
Being a bit of a thug to being a bit of a
drug smuggler to going to prison.

00:10:52.826 --> 00:10:56.328
And then I realised, you know, this is not
the life.

00:10:56.549 --> 00:11:01.533
And so I decided to go back to school and
studied law.

00:11:05.918 --> 00:11:09.780
In the time I'd spent in the world of bare
knuckle so far, I began to realise that

00:11:09.781 --> 00:11:12.561
the sport had a kind of gravitational pull
for lost souls.

00:11:13.361 --> 00:11:17.163
Many of the guys we'd spoken to seemed to
be people who'd made bad decisions in

00:11:17.203 --> 00:11:20.324
life, and perhaps in bare knuckle they'd
found a way to

00:11:20.424 --> 00:11:24.886
utilise their talents, which happened to
lay in a realm that normal society finds

00:11:24.906 --> 00:11:25.606
barbaric.

00:11:26.366 --> 00:11:30.968
However, I wondered if organised violence
was a cure or a symptom for angry young

00:11:31.008 --> 00:11:31.708
men.

00:11:32.749 --> 00:11:34.510
James Lambert

00:11:42.497 --> 00:11:47.042
Hello friends, it's James, the author of
Be Happy in 24 Hours.

00:11:47.382 --> 00:11:51.226
I used to be a very unhappy person, very
violent person, bare knuckle fighter,

00:11:51.366 --> 00:11:52.968
bouncer and unlicensed boxer.

00:11:53.348 --> 00:11:57.512
And these are some of the tips and
strategies that helped me change my life.

00:11:57.512 --> 00:12:03.313
life and literally become the happy person
I am today, helping society and being the

00:12:03.333 --> 00:12:04.033
happy coach.

00:12:04.214 --> 00:12:08.435
Retiring from the sport undefeated, James
Lambert had taken a complete U-turn from

00:12:08.455 --> 00:12:10.875
his life of violence and reinvented
himself

00:12:11.275 --> 00:12:14.796
as a lifestyle and fitness coach, calling
himself Mr Happy.

00:12:15.396 --> 00:12:16.097
How long have you lived here?

00:12:16.717 --> 00:12:17.637
Quite a while, what has it been now?

00:12:17.657 --> 00:12:19.057
I think it's coming up to two years.

00:12:19.637 --> 00:12:21.598
We've basically moved here for the peace
and quiet.

00:12:22.338 --> 00:12:25.320
And as you know, you can see it's a
cul-de-sac.

00:12:25.321 --> 00:12:27.081
It's very peaceful.

00:12:27.101 --> 00:12:28.142
We've got super neighbours.

00:12:29.063 --> 00:12:30.323
Did you want one sugar, my friend?

00:12:30.944 --> 00:12:32.685
So, were you always a fighter?

00:12:33.065 --> 00:12:35.667
There was always this fascination with
fighting.

00:12:36.027 --> 00:12:37.108
I was an unhappy, angry...

00:12:37.228 --> 00:12:37.968
violent person.

00:12:38.448 --> 00:12:43.809
I went out into the world and lo and
behold I found other angry, violent,

00:12:43.889 --> 00:12:44.730
scared young men.

00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:48.390
You know somebody would catch my eye, I
would catch theirs and a fight would

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:49.130
ensue.

00:12:49.751 --> 00:12:50.931
It was that ridiculous.

00:12:51.171 --> 00:12:52.711
Can you remember your first bare knuckle
fight?

00:12:53.291 --> 00:12:53.991
Of course.

00:12:54.072 --> 00:12:57.732
Mixed emotions even to this date because I
was terrified.

00:12:58.273 --> 00:13:03.754
I used fear as a form of energy,
transmuted that into positive energy that

00:13:03.814 --> 00:13:04.874
drove me into my

00:13:04.894 --> 00:13:05.594
victories.

00:13:05.634 --> 00:13:07.396
But again, I found it very empty.

00:13:07.516 --> 00:13:10.499
When I got home, I was still left with my
problems.

00:13:11.179 --> 00:13:13.221
Not just outside, but in my mind.

00:13:13.622 --> 00:13:17.666
So the fight did nothing to make me happy.

00:13:17.866 --> 00:13:20.528
And did you know other fighters who felt
similarly?

00:13:20.529 --> 00:13:23.131
Well, you see, this is a thing that's
never spoken about.

00:13:23.611 --> 00:13:28.816
Certainly not within that world where
emotion is immediately and very directly

00:13:28.897 --> 00:13:30.058
equated with weakness.

00:13:31.486 --> 00:13:35.907
A leopard can change its spots and that's
very important because I hear it a lot and

00:13:35.908 --> 00:13:38.168
it's a mind virus and we accept things

00:13:38.228 --> 00:13:39.148
because they're said.

00:13:39.568 --> 00:13:43.229
They're not always true, we have to
examine this and so I want you, you may be

00:13:43.230 --> 00:13:46.170
a parent and your son or daughter could be
going through difficulties

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:48.531
never give up on them, never give up on
them.

00:13:48.571 --> 00:13:51.691
Your brother, your son, your friend could
be an alcoholic a drug addict, never give

00:13:51.692 --> 00:13:52.392
up on them.

00:13:52.652 --> 00:13:56.293
People have the power to change inherently
in them I've done it myself.

00:13:56.993 --> 00:14:01.995
Even when you win, there was great pain in
my ribs could have been fractured or

00:14:02.015 --> 00:14:03.637
broken, you know, always cuts to the

00:14:03.697 --> 00:14:04.397
face.

00:14:04.417 --> 00:14:06.079
But worse than that was the mental trauma.

00:14:06.199 --> 00:14:10.764
It was realising again what I had done,
the person that I was becoming, and that

00:14:10.844 --> 00:14:12.165
really did affect me mentally.

00:14:12.365 --> 00:14:14.467
I think now looking back I became
depressed.

00:14:15.108 --> 00:14:19.993
I suppose there were thoughts, thoughts of
self-harm maybe, thoughts of actually, you

00:14:19.994 --> 00:14:22.035
know, if this is it, I

00:14:22.036 --> 00:14:25.158
don't actually want to be, I don't want
any part of this.

00:14:26.434 --> 00:14:31.479
And that was actually profoundly upsetting
for me and I felt terrible.

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:39.526
So that was actually a pretty low evening
and I'd like to say it

00:14:39.527 --> 00:14:42.068
was the last but that did happen a lot.

00:14:42.849 --> 00:14:46.392
James had removed everything that would
remind him of his past life as a violent

00:14:46.432 --> 00:14:48.554
young man, apart from a punch bag which...

00:14:48.614 --> 00:14:50.615
He still hangs in the garage where he
coaches his clients.

00:14:50.635 --> 00:14:52.096
Do you still hit the bag?

00:14:52.737 --> 00:14:54.698
Actually I've personally chosen not to.

00:14:55.979 --> 00:15:00.742
I suppose it was about two years ago when
I decided to fully refrain from fighting.

00:15:01.203 --> 00:15:04.605
And for me that's violence in word,
thought and deed.

00:15:05.065 --> 00:15:08.527
So for me, at this current point in my
life, I'm open to change.

00:15:08.528 --> 00:15:09.608
It might change next week.

00:15:10.169 --> 00:15:11.590
Other people can keep it controlled.

00:15:12.150 --> 00:15:16.173
I fear that the anger wouldn't just stay
here and again it would leak into other

00:15:16.533 --> 00:15:17.794
aspects of my life.

00:15:18.214 --> 00:15:22.017
So I've just made the personal decision to
not hit anything, if you like, for a

00:15:22.057 --> 00:15:22.757
while.

00:15:22.898 --> 00:15:24.959
And so far, I've been good to my word.

00:15:26.020 --> 00:15:30.124
Meeting James is really surprising because
here you've got a guy who's in the bare

00:15:30.125 --> 00:15:32.986
knuckle game for years and came out of it
undefeated,

00:15:33.666 --> 00:15:39.711
yet in some way he feels kind of ashamed
and he will admit that he is haunted by

00:15:39.731 --> 00:15:40.431
his past.

00:15:41.173 --> 00:15:46.137
And looking at what he does now, it seems
that his entire life is this kind of

00:15:46.557 --> 00:15:47.758
struggle to put that to bed.

00:15:48.242 --> 00:15:51.404
And he does seem to be winning that
struggle, admirably so.

00:15:51.985 --> 00:15:52.685
And the Mr.

00:15:52.685 --> 00:15:54.707
Happy thing, I guess, is a way of him
keeping that down.

00:15:55.127 --> 00:15:56.508
But behind that Mr.

00:15:56.548 --> 00:15:59.830
Happy persona, you do see flashes of the
old James.

00:16:00.231 --> 00:16:03.733
This kind of machine that used to render
men unconscious, as he said.

00:16:04.294 --> 00:16:06.615
But he will be the first to admit that.

00:16:06.895 --> 00:16:09.877
And he says that, you know, he hasn't
conquered his demons yet.

00:16:10.518 --> 00:16:15.742
Now, in this kind of suburban life,
perhaps he's fighting his biggest battle

00:16:15.743 --> 00:16:16.443
of all.

00:16:19.274 --> 00:16:23.558
The first UK vs US bare knuckle fight in
over 150 years is just days away.

00:16:24.118 --> 00:16:27.501
So we've come back to Newcastle to see
James McCrory, who's in the middle of his

00:16:27.521 --> 00:16:28.442
training preparations.

00:16:31.004 --> 00:16:31.704
Get in.

00:16:31.784 --> 00:16:32.484
Weights down.

00:16:33.005 --> 00:16:35.628
Like all my opponents, you've got to give
them a chance at the start, you know what

00:16:35.629 --> 00:16:36.329
I mean?

00:16:37.209 --> 00:16:40.011
So when you're coming out, are there any
kind of routines?

00:16:40.212 --> 00:16:44.475
Newcastle means a lot to us and Ireland
does, and I'll be wearing my Newcastle top

00:16:44.476 --> 00:16:45.376
and my Irish shorts.

00:16:47.197 --> 00:16:47.897
Bastard.

00:16:48.666 --> 00:16:50.587
Where would you like to see the sport go?

00:16:51.328 --> 00:16:52.769
Maybe 10, 15 years time, you know.

00:16:52.770 --> 00:16:55.131
It'll be hitting big arenas, you know,
but...

00:16:56.532 --> 00:16:57.232
I'll be...

00:16:57.232 --> 00:16:57.772
Well, maybe.

00:16:58.113 --> 00:16:58.813
I might not.

00:16:58.813 --> 00:17:00.895
If the money comes good, I'll look after
myself.

00:17:00.896 --> 00:17:02.596
I might still be fighting in 15 years'
time.

00:17:04.437 --> 00:17:05.458
Is that about the pressure, like?

00:17:05.459 --> 00:17:10.481
Is that about the pressure, boys?

00:17:10.482 --> 00:17:14.204
Thrive under pressure.

00:17:14.244 --> 00:17:15.144
Whoo Shaz, man, quite...

00:17:16.405 --> 00:17:17.206
Can you explain to me...

00:17:18.018 --> 00:17:19.519
What it's like in the pit?

00:17:20.280 --> 00:17:25.705
It's only like three bales are here, right
this way, three bales are here this way,

00:17:26.205 --> 00:17:26.905
and you're taking two

00:17:26.986 --> 00:17:29.708
steps into the centre, then you're there.

00:17:29.709 --> 00:17:31.710
I'd be fainting with the jab or moving my
hand about.

00:17:31.711 --> 00:17:34.712
If you can establish your jab, it's a good
thing.

00:17:34.713 --> 00:17:38.876
Then obviously you get the one-two in, and
then obviously you're going to move your

00:17:38.877 --> 00:17:41.458
head a bit, which I'd be trying to do if
someone was jabbing me.

00:17:42.258 --> 00:17:46.162
Then maybe just come and do a bit, come up
to the centre, and bang, bring a body shot

00:17:46.182 --> 00:17:46.882
in.

00:17:46.882 --> 00:17:51.066
And honestly, I'd rather have it with me
with ten in the jaw than one good one

00:17:51.086 --> 00:17:52.107
there, you know, because it really hurts.

00:17:52.287 --> 00:17:54.929
How does it feel when you get one of those
there?

00:17:54.930 --> 00:17:58.493
I can't even describe it, mate.

00:17:58.494 --> 00:18:01.956
It's the worst feeling in the world when
you can't breathe and you've got a gum

00:18:02.036 --> 00:18:02.736
shield in your mouth.

00:18:03.117 --> 00:18:06.380
You try to spit the gum shield out but you
can't because you can't get your breath to

00:18:06.381 --> 00:18:08.782
get the power out of your lungs to spit it
out.

00:18:09.743 --> 00:18:13.306
You're going red, you're starting to see
little fucking stars.

00:18:13.982 --> 00:18:16.043
Then you're going lower and lower and
lower to the ground.

00:18:16.163 --> 00:18:16.863
It's horrible.

00:18:17.024 --> 00:18:17.864
It's horrible.

00:18:18.384 --> 00:18:19.945
Eventually your hands will drop and then
boom.

00:18:20.806 --> 00:18:21.606
Good night, you know what I mean?

00:18:21.906 --> 00:18:24.928
And if I wanted to knock you out and I'm
looking for the chin about here, right?

00:18:25.028 --> 00:18:27.009
You haven't brought your 14-pound hammer
here, mate.

00:18:27.649 --> 00:18:28.590
So you're all fucking out of luck.

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:30.611
You mentioned being punch drunk earlier.

00:18:30.671 --> 00:18:33.433
Do you think you could have a wake-up call
at all?

00:18:33.453 --> 00:18:36.854
I've had some great nights with the boxing
and with Ben Otter.

00:18:37.135 --> 00:18:39.396
If I wasn't so brain damaged, I could tell
you that Marley and I...

00:18:39.896 --> 00:18:41.777
Do you worry it might affect your memories
of your family?

00:18:41.957 --> 00:18:43.118
Those kind of important...

00:18:43.774 --> 00:18:44.474
What moments

00:18:50.980 --> 00:18:53.682
were heavy?

00:18:53.683 --> 00:18:55.764
Well, probably already has, you know.

00:18:55.765 --> 00:18:58.546
I mean, I can remember the day that my dad
died.

00:18:59.047 --> 00:19:01.509
I can remember it all, every single second
of it.

00:19:02.330 --> 00:19:05.492
But I can't remember much otherwise.

00:19:05.493 --> 00:19:08.615
I could get hit by a bus, you know, and I
wouldn't have any memories at all.

00:19:08.655 --> 00:19:10.196
So it's just a risk you've got to take,
isn't it?

00:19:10.216 --> 00:19:12.118
That's why the tattoo's on my back, you
know.

00:19:12.594 --> 00:19:15.897
McCrory is a Catholic cross, the shamrock
for my dad in Nerfia.

00:19:16.597 --> 00:19:17.859
I'm going to be scared now in life, man.

00:19:17.879 --> 00:19:19.940
You just go for it, whatever happens,
happens.

00:19:20.421 --> 00:19:23.143
There's a lot more better fighters than
there's out there, but the difference,

00:19:23.523 --> 00:19:24.965
I've got the balls to fucking...

00:19:25.385 --> 00:19:26.506
I don't just talk about it.

00:19:26.886 --> 00:19:29.268
If I say I'll turn for a fight, I'll turn
for a fight, doesn't matter where I go.

00:19:29.849 --> 00:19:35.573
I don't think Leanne and my mother realise
just how big a part of this is in my life.

00:19:36.034 --> 00:19:38.756
It's fucking great when you can take
someone's best digs and you can give them

00:19:38.796 --> 00:19:40.718
your best and see who comes out better.

00:19:41.782 --> 00:19:45.869
From spending time with James, what I
really began to understand was this idea

00:19:45.870 --> 00:19:46.570
of heart.

00:19:46.631 --> 00:19:48.614
I think a lot of us throw it out as like a
kind of...

00:19:49.154 --> 00:19:53.097
Just a cliche, but actually looking at
James and the way he conducts his life

00:19:53.577 --> 00:19:55.758
with this kind of very emotional attitude

00:19:56.178 --> 00:20:00.801
towards the death of his father and his
relationship with his family and what he

00:20:00.821 --> 00:20:03.082
does is he managed to channel that and
bring

00:20:03.083 --> 00:20:03.783
it into the ring.

00:20:04.003 --> 00:20:05.243
He breaks every cliche.

00:20:05.604 --> 00:20:08.945
I mean he's not one of these guys who
comes around toting his unbeaten record.

00:20:09.286 --> 00:20:13.008
He knows he's been beaten a few times and
he literally takes it on the chin and

00:20:13.009 --> 00:20:15.809
accepts that And maybe he's the perfect
fighter

00:20:16.149 --> 00:20:17.070
because he's fallible.

00:20:21.122 --> 00:20:22.443
I love fighting.

00:20:22.444 --> 00:20:24.644
I'm the American that's coming over here
across the Atlantic.

00:20:24.645 --> 00:20:25.445
I mean, it's a big deal.

00:20:25.925 --> 00:20:26.885
I don't think I'm going to lose.

00:20:27.386 --> 00:20:30.087
That's not even in my mindset, you know,
it's not even an option to me.

00:20:31.048 --> 00:20:32.449
You know, I've been a fighter my whole
life.

00:20:32.609 --> 00:20:34.590
I feel like I'm the more skilled fighter.

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:36.011
I'm the bigger fighter.

00:20:36.812 --> 00:20:39.773
I don't really give a damn what anybody
says because people are always going to

00:20:39.774 --> 00:20:40.474
have opinions.

00:20:40.474 --> 00:20:41.354
People are always going to doubt you.

00:20:41.614 --> 00:20:42.314
None of that matters.

00:20:42.314 --> 00:20:44.016
What matters is what happens in that pit
when it's me and him.

00:20:44.356 --> 00:20:46.557
Me and James, I'm very ready to go.

00:20:54.046 --> 00:20:56.667
It was the bare-knuckle extravaganza down
in South London.

00:20:57.287 --> 00:21:00.608
The US vs UK Transatlantic Showdown.

00:21:01.049 --> 00:21:02.989
The biggest bare-knuckle fight in recent
history.

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:11.152
Two champions, one from America, one from
the UK, fighting this

00:21:13.593 --> 00:21:14.293
belt.

00:21:14.293 --> 00:21:20.556
Two times since 1863 and this belt is

00:21:20.557 --> 00:21:21.257
impossible.

00:21:21.257 --> 00:21:21.896
But before the title fight, we were
treated to a few other terrors.

00:21:21.896 --> 00:21:23.596
tear ups in the build up to the main
event.

00:21:24.137 --> 00:21:26.137
It was a festival of physical abuse.

00:21:26.697 --> 00:21:28.097
Blood, guts, glory.

00:21:28.177 --> 00:21:30.318
I want to see people going for it.

00:21:36.359 --> 00:21:38.880
Bare knuckle, it is the ultimate sport.

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:40.400
Yeah, ultimate tear up.

00:21:40.540 --> 00:21:45.521
Just enjoy getting in there, you know,
real punches and no fucking around, you

00:21:45.522 --> 00:21:46.222
know what I mean?

00:21:49.842 --> 00:21:51.823
There's no old barbed wire left, you know.

00:21:51.883 --> 00:21:53.463
They really go for it.

00:21:53.823 --> 00:21:55.984
Violence and plenty of chances of getting
back at you.

00:22:07.308 --> 00:22:08.528
Fucking good buzz, you know what I mean?

00:22:08.529 --> 00:22:10.629
It's one of the best buzzes I've ever had,
you know what I mean?

00:22:10.989 --> 00:22:12.470
It's up there with sex, my friend.

00:22:15.002 --> 00:22:17.445
England is the home of bare knuckle.

00:22:17.446 --> 00:22:19.127
I think the British, it's in the blood.

00:22:30.886 --> 00:22:31.586
We're all day, man.

00:22:31.586 --> 00:22:32.387
You know what I mean?

00:22:32.388 --> 00:22:33.687
Fuck the fucking rest of the world.

00:22:34.287 --> 00:22:35.448
Salt Lake City, Utah.

00:22:35.449 --> 00:22:37.929
I'm here for Jason the Machine Gun Young,
USA.

00:22:38.209 --> 00:22:41.370
Jason the Machine Gun Young, fighting for
the Atlanta Heavyweight title against the

00:22:41.390 --> 00:22:43.651
UK champ James Justybill McCrory, and I'm
ready to kick his ass.

00:22:44.151 --> 00:22:46.532
Jason was everything you'd expect an
American fighter to be.

00:22:47.132 --> 00:22:49.673
Brash, verbose, and massively patriotic.

00:22:49.933 --> 00:22:52.634
He'd even referred to himself as the bald
eagle on a few occasions.

00:22:55.130 --> 00:22:57.792
Unfortunately today's bare-knuckle boxers
are mostly just boxers.

00:22:57.953 --> 00:22:58.913
I bring a different style.

00:22:59.394 --> 00:23:00.214
For me it's natural.

00:23:01.616 --> 00:23:05.079
I tune everything else out, the crowd, the
noise, the cameras, everything, and just

00:23:05.119 --> 00:23:05.899
focus on my opponent.

00:23:06.140 --> 00:23:06.860
Just in the zone.

00:23:08.682 --> 00:23:11.905
I'm the first American to come over here
since 1863 and fight for the title, so

00:23:12.325 --> 00:23:13.486
there's much more pressure on him.

00:23:14.146 --> 00:23:17.870
Because I'm the unknown, I'm coming for
the United States, we have a huge

00:23:17.890 --> 00:23:18.590
advantage.

00:23:18.610 --> 00:23:22.454
It was 10 o'clock, the scheduled time for
the fight, but James was still nowhere to

00:23:22.455 --> 00:23:23.155
be seen.

00:23:23.974 --> 00:23:27.055
Rumors that he was refusing to come down
was spreading throughout the crowd.

00:23:27.975 --> 00:23:31.636
Some said he was in a cab on his way from
Newcastle, others said he bottled it.

00:23:32.577 --> 00:23:36.258
This didn't sound like the James I knew,
but time was ticking on, and the success

00:23:36.259 --> 00:23:38.098
of the night depended on his appearance.

00:23:39.639 --> 00:23:43.500
Jason, who'd been in training for weeks,
had become increasingly agitated.

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:46.341
Well, I don't know what happened.

00:23:46.342 --> 00:23:47.561
He got stuck up in Newcastle.

00:23:47.881 --> 00:23:49.742
I mean, we've known about this fight for a
very long time.

00:23:49.743 --> 00:23:50.782
I came all the way from America.

00:23:51.238 --> 00:23:53.339
If I was back in America, I'd have a
hundred friends who would come get me

00:23:53.340 --> 00:23:54.499
immediately and bring my ass down here.

00:23:54.940 --> 00:23:57.381
So I basically just told them, you know,
get down here.

00:23:57.761 --> 00:23:59.742
Seems like there's a lot of excuses with
today's fighters.

00:24:00.002 --> 00:24:02.743
Back in the day, somebody called somebody
out and, you know, if you're going to be

00:24:02.783 --> 00:24:04.944
disrespectful, you've got to back it up.

00:24:05.744 --> 00:24:08.505
People were beginning to lose hope and
headed towards the exit.

00:24:09.486 --> 00:24:12.627
It was looking likely that history
wouldn't be made tonight.

00:24:15.068 --> 00:24:17.989
And suddenly, like the angel of the north,
he rose.

00:24:19.050 --> 00:24:19.770
James McCrory.

00:24:20.290 --> 00:24:24.393
A few stones heavier, a few inches to his
beard and wearing a Newcastle football

00:24:24.394 --> 00:24:25.615
shirt had arrived.

00:24:26.595 --> 00:24:30.018
Looking slightly bleary eyed, he'd fallen
asleep for the entire cab journey.

00:24:31.059 --> 00:24:34.502
But was he too tired, too full of Guinness
to take on the machine gun?

00:24:40.187 --> 00:24:44.290
After weeks of build up, training, mind
games and the threat of one of them not

00:24:44.350 --> 00:24:47.073
even turning up, the Atlantic title fight
was about

00:24:47.074 --> 00:24:47.774
to start.

00:24:48.254 --> 00:24:48.954
We were here.

00:24:48.954 --> 00:24:54.419
Here on the Edge of History, America
versus the UK, toe to toe, bare knuckle.

00:25:21.982 --> 00:25:26.048
As the machine guns fist hammered down on
the struggling gypsy boy, it seemed that

00:25:26.049 --> 00:25:28.431
the title might be heading across the
Atlantic.

00:25:34.038 --> 00:25:35.861
But McCrory had other ideas.

00:26:12.402 --> 00:26:13.102
Done it.

00:26:13.763 --> 00:26:17.746
James McCrory have made sure that Britain
have won the bare knuckle bragging rights

00:26:18.406 --> 00:26:20.728
and Young and his entourage were on their
way back to

00:26:20.828 --> 00:26:22.809
Utah with their tails between their legs.

00:26:27.693 --> 00:26:31.816
His victory marked a step into the big
time not just for Andy Topliffe's company

00:26:32.476 --> 00:26:33.797
but for bare knuckle as a sport.

00:26:35.570 --> 00:26:39.315
And perhaps it had moved closer to
everyone's dream of it becoming the

00:26:39.355 --> 00:26:42.540
biggest, nastiest and most exciting blood
sport in the

00:26:42.600 --> 00:26:43.300
UK.

